\"text\": \"As he grew taller, his dominance on the court became apparent, and it wasn't long before college scouts from the United States took notice.\"}, {\"id\": \"s6\", \"text\": \"In 2013, Mamadou made the bold decision to leave his homeland and pursue his basketball dreams in the United States.\"}, {\"id\": \"s7\", \"text\": \"He enrolled at Stoneridge Prep in Simi Valley, California, where he would spend a year refining his game and adapting to the American style of play.\"}, {\"id\": \"s8\", \"text\": \"It was during this time that he caught the attention of college coaches, including those from the University of California, Irvine.\"}, {\"id\": \"s9\", \"text\": \"UC Irvine, a mid-major program with a growing reputation, saw immense potential in the 7-foot-6 center.\"}, {\"id\": \"s10\", \"text\": \"They offered him a scholarship, and Mamadou accepted, becoming the tallest player in the program's history.\"}, {\"id\": \"s11\", \"text\": \"As he donned the Anteaters' uniform, he brought with him a unique set of skills, including his imposing presence in the paint and a soft touch around the rim.\"}, {\"id\": \"s12\", \"text\": \"Mamadou's impact was immediate.\"}, {\"id\": \"s13\", \"text\": \"In his freshman year, he averaged 10.5 points, 7.1 rebounds, and 2.4 blocks per game, earning him Big West Conference Freshman of the Year honors.\"}, {\"id\": \"s14\", \"text\": \"His dominance continued throughout his collegiate career, as he led the Anteaters to multiple postseason appearances and set numerous program records.\"}, {\"id\": \"s15\", \"text\": \"One of the most compelling pieces of evidence supporting Mamadou's affiliation with UC Irvine is his impressive statistical record.\"}, {\"id\": \"s16\", \"text\": \"According to the NCAA, Mamadou played in 127 games for the Anteaters, averaging 9.4 points, 6.4 rebounds, and 2.1 blocks per game.\"}]}"
